{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he dreamed, and behold, etc.</b> The reason He said <b>and behold</b>: since a dream is not definitively in the category of truth, for dreams are vanity, and besides, they always contain some chaff, for they are in the appearance of confusion — therefore He said ״וְהִנֵּה״ — meaning, that the matters were without confusion and imaginings, but rather every thing was revealed to him and clear as the shining of day, and this is not like other dreams in which one sees a thing but does not determine in his vision what he is seeing. And therefore you will find that He was precise to say, for each and every detail revealed to him in the dream, ״וְהִנֵּה״: concerning the seeing of the ladder He said <b>and behold</b> a ladder; concerning the seeing of the angels He said <b>and behold</b> angels of, etc.; concerning the revelation of the Shekhinah He said <b>and behold</b> HaShem — the intention in this is that it was actual prophecy."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:13.962769206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}